{% extends "layout.html.twig" %}

{% block content %}
    <section class="hero is-info is-bold mb-5">
        <div class="hero-body">
            <div class="container">
                <h1 class="title">
                    {{ 'Welcome to VerteXVaaR.BlueSprints'|t }}
                </h1>
                <h2 class="subtitle">
                    {{ 'An experiment gone right :D'|t }}
                </h2>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="box">
        <div class="content">
            <p>
                {{ 'VerteXVaaR.BlueSprints was created in a few hours as an experiment of "what could be done in 3 hours" and it\'s development continued for 6 other hours. After 9 hours it had (all simple) routing, templating, of course autoloading (thanks composer) and NoDB persistence, all out of the box. But more is to come.'|t }}
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="columns is-multiline">
        <div class="column is-6">
            <div class="card">
                <header class="card-header">
                    <p class="card-header-title">{{ 'It will stay simple!'|t }}</p>
                </header>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <div class="content">
                        <p>
                            {{ 'This PHP Framework is designed to stay as simple as possible but yet provide some indispensable features.'|t }}
                            {{ 'Features included (packages in braces are optional)'|t }}:
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>{{ 'Dependency Injection (PSR-11 "Container Interface") backend by Symfony Dependency Injection'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ 'File based storage solution for entities'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ 'Caching (PSR-16 "Simple Caching")'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueweb) Routing configured by annotations'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueweb) Standardized Request/Response system (PSR-7: "HTTP message interfaces")'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueweb) Middlewares (PSR-15: "HTTP Server Request Handlers")'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueweb) Templating with Twig'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueweb) Controller action caching by annotation'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/bluescheduler) Scheduling configured by Annotations'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/bluetranslation) i18n (translations) backend by Symfony Translation'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueauth) Username/Password Authentication'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueauth) Users management via CLI'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/blueconsole) Console Application backend by Symfony Console'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/bluedebug) Debugging toolbar'|t }}</li>
                            <li>{{ '(vertexvaar/bluelog) Logging integration with Sentry and Docker support'|t }}</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>
                            {{ 'Features not included (and probably not about to be)'|t }}
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>{{ 'Database Connections'|t }}</li>
                            <li>ORMs</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="column is-6">
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <header class="card-header">
                    <p class="card-header-title">{{ 'Fast framework, fast Development'|t }}</p>
                </header>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <div class="content">
                        <p>
                            Because there are almost no classes inside vertexvaar/bluesprints, and it has no reflection
                            or abstraction
                            it is simply fast by design, without any caching. This (nearly) slender design is good for
                            performance, but
                            it prevents some features. But if you want to develop a simple Application that stores a few
                            models or just
                            prints out content you will be convinced by your own development speed
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
                <header class="card-header">
                    <p class="card-header-title">Templating</p>
                </header>
                <div class="card-content">
                    <div class="content">
                        <p>
                            Templating might be something you have don't have to get used to, because it uses Twig. Here
                            is some data
                            set by the controller:
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            {% for string in strings %}
                                <li>{{ string }}</li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="columns">
        <div class="column">
            <article class="message is-success">
                <div class="message-header">
                    <p>Persistence?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="message-body">
                    Want a demo about Persistence? Just <b><a href="/fruits">follow me</a></b> ;)
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <article class="message is-warning">
                <div class="message-header">
                    <p>Caching?</p>
                </div>
                <div class="message-body">
                    Want a demo about Caching? You can set and retrieve cached values <a href="/cache/index">here</a> ;)
                    <br>
                    More interested in caching of controller actions? <a href="/cached">This action</a> is cached!
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="box">
        <h2 class="title is-4">Session? Login?</h2>
        <div class="content">
            <p>
                bluesprints can be easily extended with a username/password login by requiring vertexvaar/blueauth.
                blueauth contains all files required for a full authentication workflow.
                Create users with <code>bin/blueconsole app:user:create [user] [pass]</code>.
                User sessions are automatically checked via middleware. You can access the session from the request
                object.
            </p>
        </div>

        {% if session is defined and session.authenticated %}
            <div class="notification is-success">
                You are currently authenticated as <strong>{{ session.username }}</strong>. Your session identifier
                is <code>{{ session.identifier }}</code>
                <br>
                <a class="button is-light mt-2" href="/logout">Click here to log out</a>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <div class="notification is-info">
                Login with your created user <a class="button is-primary is-light ml-2" href="/login">Login</a>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
